uare, preventing White from playing e4 easily\n- It prepares kingside castling (after developing the f8 bishop)\n- It follows the fundamental opening principle: "Knights before bishops"\n- It doesn\'t create weaknesses or expose valuable pieces prematurely\n- This is a classical response in many openings and gives Black a solid, flexible position\n\n**Answer: N: g8-f6**'}
