ritical weakness at f2, defended only by the king. With both White knights on the 5th rank and no piece defending f2, Qh4 creates an immediate checkmate threat that White must address. This puts Black in the driver's seat and punishes White's overly aggressive knight development.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
