, or castle queenside.\n\n**Reason:** \nDelivering check with tempo while developing a piece is a fundamental chess principle. The white king's exposed position on f2 makes this check particularly strong, forcing White into a defensive posture while I improve my piece coordination.\n\n**Answer:** B: f8-b4"}
